\">As of Oct 12, the record for Washington County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids May to June and June to July each came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years. In 2025 the county&rsquo;s middle value got 147% of normal in May to June and 26% in November to December. Grid 12136 had its driest year in 2011 at 50% of normal.</p>"}
